{#-
  Lido — mint wstETH from ETH.

  Scopes the one-way conversion WETH → ETH → stETH → wstETH. This is the
  collateral-acquisition leg of a leveraged wstETH/WETH position: `submit`
  mints stETH at Lido's exchange rate with no market involved, so the leg
  carries no slippage and needs no price checker.

  Required template params:
    (none)

  Optional params:
    max_approval — exclusive upper bound (in wei) for the stETH `approve`
                   amount, emitted as `less_than max_approval`. Defaults to
                   uint256.max, which only rules out the literal
                   infinite-approval sentinel and does NOT bound exposure.
                   Set it to a realistic operational ceiling.

  Resolved from aliases (NOT params):
    aliases.tokens.WETH   — WETH, unwrapped to ETH
    aliases.tokens.stETH  — Lido's stETH; also the staking entrypoint
    aliases.tokens.wstETH — the wstETH wrapper
    aliases.ZERO          — auto-injected, used to pin the referral

  The three addresses are fixed by the protocol, so none of them is a param:
  there is nothing for a deployment to choose. The reverse direction
  (`unwrap`, or Lido's withdrawal queue) is deliberately absent — exits go
  through a swap venue, which is scoped by its own template.

  Policy enforced:
    WETH.withdraw(amount)          amount pass
    stETH.submit(referral)         referral == aliases.ZERO,
                                   execution_options: "send"
    stETH.approve(wstETH, amount)  spender pinned to the wrapper,
                                   amount < max_approval
    wstETH.wrap(amount)            amount pass

  Four things worth knowing about this policy:

  `submit` is the only value-bearing call in the repo, hence the `send`
  execution option. Send permits attaching ETH and says nothing about how
  much. The amount is unbounded here because of a ZAC gap, not a platform
  limitation: Roles V2 does have an ether allowance, surfaced by the pinned
  SDK as `etherWithinAllowance` in the very options object where zac writes
  `send`, but the DSL has no allowance operator and `executionFlags` maps
  only `send` and `delegatecall`. So the value is bounded by the Safe's ETH
  balance alone. That is the mechanism to reach for if a future policy needs
  a real ceiling — do not conclude from this template that none exists.

  The unbounded amount is acceptable here because the destination is pinned
  to stETH, which mints to `msg.sender`: the Safe converts its own ETH into
  its own stETH, so a compromised role member can change the Safe's asset
  mix but cannot move value to an address it does not control. The
  conversion is one-way under this policy — nothing here routes back to
  WETH — so the exit belongs to a swap venue's own template. Do not reuse
  `send` against a target that can forward funds elsewhere without
  re-examining all of this.

  The referral is pinned to the zero address rather than left to the caller.
  Lido pays referral rewards to whoever is named, so an unpinned parameter
  would let a role member redirect a benefit away from the vault on every
  mint, without ever failing the gate.

  `max_approval` bounds the STANDING allowance, not cumulative volume.
  `approve` overwrites rather than increments and `increaseAllowance` is not
  scoped, so the allowance itself can never exceed the ceiling. But `wrap`
  takes any amount and nothing rate-limits the approve-then-wrap loop, so
  total wrapped volume is unbounded whatever the ceiling is set to. Bounding
  the loop would need `callWithinAllowance`, which the DSL cannot express
  either. If `increaseAllowance` is ever added here, the ceiling becomes
  bypassable by repeated increments.

  One rendering note: `withdraw` and `wrap` have `pass` on their only
  parameter, so the plan emits them as selector-only (wildcarded) grants.
  Their `params:` blocks constrain nothing beyond the selector — which is
  what `pass` means, but it reads like a constraint.
-#}
roles:
  - address: "{{ aliases.tokens.WETH }}"
    functions:
      - signature: "function withdraw(uint256 amount)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: amount
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "pass"

  - address: "{{ aliases.tokens.stETH }}"
    functions:
      - signature: "function submit(address referral)"
        execution_options: "send"
        params:
          - name: referral
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "equal_to"
            value: "{{ aliases.ZERO }}"
            value_type: "address"

      - signature: "function approve(address spender, uint256 amount)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: spender
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "equal_to"
            value: "{{ aliases.tokens.wstETH }}"
            value_type: "address"
          - name: amount
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "less_than"
            value: "{{ max_approval | default('115792089237316195423570985008687907853269984665640564039457584007913129639935') }}"
            value_type: "uint256"

  - address: "{{ aliases.tokens.wstETH }}"
    functions:
      - signature: "function wrap(uint256 amount)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: amount
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "pass"
